Hello all,

What is the actual definition of abundance used in distsamp?

When I estimate density, I get a number that I can pass on to land managers and tell them that there are ~130 individuals per hectare at site X. I like the straight forward interpretation of that number. But I don't understand what exactly the abundance estimate means. Any insight would be greatly appreciated.

Chris

From u527e14923215b7e4 at groups.google.com  Tue Jan 17 18:57:15 2012
From: u527e14923215b7e4 at groups.google.com (Richard Chandler)
Date: Tue, 17 Jan 2012 18:57:15 +0000
Subject: Re: [unmarked] Definition of abundance
Message-ID: <vStuwCdk7WQ.I37p_AxHkUoJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <vStuwCdk7WQ.hD4oFZiq_LsJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
References: <vStuwCdk7WQ.hD4oFZiq_LsJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/vStuwCdk7WQ/m/I37p_AxHkUoJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Chris,

The estimate you get from distsamp when output="abund" is simply the expected number of individuals/plot. If you recorded data out to 100 meters, then the estimate would be the expected number of individuals in a 100 meter radius plot. Density is just N/plot area.

Richard

